    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0561" n="547" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg547"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.01/8–21744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-01T22:00:00-04:00">September 1,
                            1944—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2430. The question of whether or not Germany is to be partitioned is currently
                    under consideration and has not yet been decided.<anchor n="97" xml:id="d313-f1"
                    /> It appears, however, that the territorial arrangement outlined in your SS–2,
                    August 27, 5 p.m., would not fit in with Allied plans in so far as they have
                    been formulated up to the present time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d313-f1" n="97" xml:id="d313-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence on the problem of the partition of Germany, see <ref
                        target="#pg161">pp. 161</ref>–<ref target="#pg166">166</ref>, <ref
